# busybox crond, one line, no daemon of its own.
#
# `zmrig-os sync` exits in microseconds when the last check-in was too recent,
# so this is not "poll every minute" in any way that costs a rig anything: an
# idle rig makes one small HTTPS request a minute and a busy one makes exactly
# the same. It also means the bot can act within a minute of a button press,
# which is the difference between a fleet tool and a log viewer.
* * * * * /usr/local/bin/zmrig-os sync --quiet
